---
import { btnCls, cardCls, crumbCls, emptyCls, fieldCls, rangeCls, selectCls, tabCls, tabsCls } from '../lib/ui';
// One class of ship (a model size): the template every class on the ladder uses (UI.md, "Model pages"). It lives at
// #/classes/<class>[/overview|/training|/scoring|/waypoints] and has five tabs of its own:
//   Fleet     the ships of this class (the default)
//   Overview  the model's performance in as few charts as possible
//   Training  what it was trained on and how: the model, every run's setup, loss, the shelves
//   Scoring   every score on its runs, in two parts: science (how well it predicts text it has
//             never seen) and art (how its writing compares with real books)
//   Waypoints the moments it passes in training: Nevermores (induction heads) forming, traits emerging
// A panel that belongs to one kind of model only carries data-kind (the proxy's calibration).
---
<div class="section" id="rung">
  <h1><a class={crumbCls('back')} href="#/classes">← classes</a> <span id="rungtitle"></span> <span class="q" id="rungjob"></span></h1>
  <nav class={tabsCls('line', 'subnav')} data-orientation="horizontal" data-variant="line" id="modelnav">
    <a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-mtab="fleet">Fleet</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-mtab="goals">Goals</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-mtab="overview">Overview</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-mtab="training">Training</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-mtab="scoring">Scoring</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-mtab="waypoints">Waypoints</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-mtab="fitouts">Fitouts</a>
  </nav>

  <!-- ============================== Fleet: the ships of this class -->
  <div class="mtab" data-mtab="fleet">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>The fleet <span class="note">every ship of this class: a ship is the class fitted out one way (its training material and settings), and its voyages are its runs, one per seed; open one to see it sail</span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="fleettable" class="clickable"><thead><tr><th>ship</th><th>fitout</th><th>voyages</th><th>expedition</th><th>status</th>
        <th>Forgotten Tomes (mean)</th><th>best</th><th>last sailed</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
      <details class="archive" id="fleetarchivewrap"><summary>The First Fleet <span class="note" id="fleetarchivesum"></span></summary>
        <div class="scroll"><table id="fleetarchive" class="clickable"><thead><tr><th>ship</th><th>fitout</th><th>voyages</th><th>expedition</th><th>status</th>
          <th>Forgotten Tomes (mean)</th><th>best</th><th>last sailed</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></details>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================== Goals: this class on the route to quantum physics -->
  <div class="mtab" data-mtab="goals">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><div class="rungover" id="goalsover"></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>Filling the seven steps <span class="note">the goal: as many tricks as this ship can learn, building on everything below it, so the route fills as fast as it can. Green is performed by this class, outlined is inherited from a smaller class (carried up, still to show here), grey is open</span></h2>
      <div class="coverage" id="goalcoverage"></div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>On the route to quantum physics <span class="note">the seven waypoints, bottom to top; the tricks the field expects of this size are lit, those it carries up from smaller classes are marked, and those the field expects only of bigger classes are faded: still worth taking. ◆ is a gate: performed before a ship moves on to the next waypoint. Open a trick for its stars and progress</span></h2>
      <div class="goalroute" id="goalroute"></div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>What the field expects of this size <span class="note">the minimum, not the limit: the tricks the field would expect a ship this size to reach, and how its voyages are doing on each; every trick above them is worth taking too. Sort by any column, filter by step</span></h2>
      <div class="handtools"><span class="note">step to quantum physics</span><select class={selectCls('')} id="goalfilter" title="filter the goals by waypoint"><option value="">all seven</option></select></div>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="goaltable" class="clickable"><thead><tr><th>trick</th><th>waypoint</th><th>gate</th><th>rests on</th><th>the field shows it at</th><th>on this class</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================== Overview -->
  <div class="mtab" data-mtab="overview">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="gridpanel">
      <h2>Every voyage at this size <span class="note">one square per voyage in the order they started; the brighter the green, the better (lower) its Forgotten Tomes bits per byte, by quartile of the voyages scored so far; an outlined square is running</span></h2>
      <div id="rungridsum" class="gridsum"></div>
      <div id="rungrid"></div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>The Forgotten Tomes score, voyage by voyage <span class="note">bits per byte on 16 books Qwen 3.8 cannot have read, lower is better; one dot per scored voyage in the order they started, the line is the best so far, dotted lines are Qwen models scored the same way</span></h2>
      <div class="chart tall" id="ftchart"></div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================== Training -->
  <div class="mtab" data-mtab="training">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><div class="rungover" id="rungover"></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>The voyages <span class="note">each voyage's library, passes and settings, and how far it got <b class="recentnote"></b></span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="trainruns" class="clickable"><thead><tr><th>ship</th><th>name</th><th>status</th><th>library</th><th>passes</th><th>seed</th>
        <th>vocab</th><th>context</th><th>tokens seen</th><th>minutes</th><th>started</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>Training loss <span class="note">nats per token on the training library, the latest 12 voyages at this size</span></h2>
      <div class="chart" id="losschart"></div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>The training libraries <span class="note">every book a voyage read; click one to read it, the same stripped text Thorp trains on</span></h2>
      <div class="booktabs"><select class={selectCls('')} id="shelfpick" title="the voyage whose library is shown"></select><input class={fieldCls('')} id="bookfilter" placeholder="filter by title or family"></div>
      <div class="scroll bookswrap"><table id="shelftable" class="clickable"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================== Scoring -->
  <div class="mtab" data-mtab="scoring">
    <h2 class="band">Science <span class="q">how well it predicts text it has never seen: bits per byte, lower is better</span></h2>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>What we measure <span class="note">"to come" is not built yet</span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="sciencemetrics"><thead><tr><th>metric</th><th>what it tells us</th><th>better is</th><th>state</th><th id="scorenowhead">now</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Scoreboard <span class="note">the Forgotten Tomes and the voyage's English held-out books, then the held-out score by kind of byte <b class="recentnote"></b></span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="scienceboard"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="calpanel" data-kind="proxy" hidden>
      <h2>Calibration against 9m <span class="note">the same library and passes at both sizes; the proxy is trusted only if it orders the libraries as 9m does. Forgotten Tomes bits per byte, English, lower is better</span></h2>
      <div class="row">
        <div class="scroll"><table id="caltable"><thead><tr><th>library</th><th>passes</th><th>9m voyage</th><th>9m score</th><th>1m voyage</th><th>1m score</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table>
          <p class="note" id="calverdict"></p></div>
        <div class="chart" id="calchart"></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Bits per byte by kind of byte <span class="note">spelling is "inside a word"; one bar per voyage; lower is better</span></h2><div class="chart" id="splitchart"></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>The Forgotten Tomes, book by book <span class="note">the best voyage at this size, the latest voyages and Qwen; click a book to read it</span></h2>
      <div class="scroll bookswrap"><table id="tomestable" class="clickable"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>

    <h2 class="band">Art <span class="q">how its writing compares with real books: the laws of text, grammar, voice</span></h2>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>What we measure <span class="note">"to come" is not built yet</span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="artmetrics"><thead><tr><th>metric</th><th>what it tells us</th><th>better is</th><th>state</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Scoreboard <span class="note">the laws on the text it writes, model beside the books' own value (ref) <b class="recentnote"></b></span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="artboard"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>The laws: model against the books <span class="note">model value ÷ the books' value; closer to the dotted line at 1 is better</span></h2><div class="chart" id="lawchart"></div></section>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================== Waypoints -->
  <div class="mtab" data-mtab="fitouts">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>Fitouts <span class="note">the training material curated for this class, matched to its stages: pretraining (in order, one voyage) and post-training (in order, each seeded from the one before); then the four necessary cards each stage has drawn so far, voyage by voyage</span></h2>
      <div id="classfitouts"><div class={emptyCls()}>reading the fitouts…</div></div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <div class="mtab" data-mtab="waypoints">
    <!-- the three steps a class proves in order: match the field, beat it at this size, then reach up -->
    <nav class={tabsCls('line', 'subnav')} data-orientation="horizontal" data-variant="line" id="wpnav"><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-wsub="expected">1 · Expected</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-wsub="envelope">2 · Pushing the envelope</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-wsub="stars">3 · Exploring the stars</a></nav>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><div class="wpsteps" id="wpsteps"></div>
      <div class="handtools mt"><span class="note">step to quantum physics</span><select class={selectCls('')} id="wpfilter" title="filter the tricks by waypoint"><option value="">all seven</option></select></div></section>
    <div class="wsub" data-wsub="expected">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Expected <span class="note">what the field already shows at this size or smaller: the tricks to prove first, so the ship is known to match the field before it tries to beat it</span></h2>
        <div class="scroll"><table id="wp-expected" class="clickable"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    </div>
    <div class="wsub" data-wsub="envelope">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Pushing the envelope <span class="note">this class's goals, and those it carries up from smaller classes, that nobody has shown at this size: the field shows them only in bigger models</span></h2>
        <div class="scroll"><table id="wp-envelope" class="clickable"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    </div>
    <div class="wsub" data-wsub="stars">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Exploring the stars <span class="note">the ambitious tricks: goals of the bigger classes, nearest first. A ship of this class performing one is a find</span></h2>
        <div class="scroll"><table id="wp-stars" class="clickable"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    </div>

    <h2 class="band">The instruments <span class="q">the stars, Nevermores and traits as measured on this class's voyages, behind the tricks above</span></h2>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>Stars in reach <span class="note">the kinds of head this class is expected to reach (the star chart's "expected from" at or below it), and how its own voyages are doing on each; <span id="reachnext"></span></span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="reachtable"><thead><tr><th>kind of head</th><th>family</th><th>expected from</th><th>why</th><th>on this class</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>Waypoints, voyage by voyage <span class="note">the training step at which each voyage first passed each waypoint; "not yet" is measured but not reached, – is not measured on that voyage <b class="recentnote"></b></span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="waypointtable"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>
    <h2 class="band">Nevermores <span class="q">induction heads: at a word seen before, a head looks back to what followed it last time and bets it comes again; they form suddenly</span><span class="bandtools"><button class={btnCls('outline', '')} data-essay="nevermore">Read: what a Nevermore is</button><button class={btnCls('outline', '')} id="readpassage">Read the test passage</button></span></h2>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="handpanel">
      <h2>The hand <span class="note">each card is one attention head, rows by layer from the top; a card turns face up (♠) when its head becomes a Nevermore, 0.3 or more on either test; until then its face shows through as far as the head has come. The big number is the real-prose score, the corner one the random test. Bigger models show their strongest five</span></h2>
      <div class="handtools"><select class={selectCls('')} id="handrun" title="the voyage whose hand is shown"></select>
        <button class={btnCls('outline', '')} id="handplay" title="deal the hand step by step">▶ play</button>
        <input class={rangeCls('')} type="range" id="handstep" min="0" max="0" value="0"><span id="handlabel"></span></div>
      <div id="hand"></div>
    </section>
    <div class="row">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>The strongest head <span class="note">its Nevermore score on a real passage read twice, by training step (where one shows first); the line crossing 0.3 is the moment a Nevermore forms; the latest 12 voyages</span></h2><div class="chart" id="nvchart"></div></section>
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Copy gain <span class="note">nats per token the model saves on the second copy of a sequence, which only a model that copies can; higher is better</span></h2><div class="chart" id="copychart"></div></section>
    </div>
    <h2 class="band">Traits <span class="q">can its hidden state tell fiction, verse and first person apart on books it has never read; found at the dotted line, learned when it also clears the bag-of-tokens and untrained-model floors</span><span class="bandtools"><button class={btnCls('outline', '')} data-essay="traits">Read: how traits are found</button></span></h2>
    <div class="row3">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Fiction</h2><div class="chart short" id="trait-fiction"></div></section>
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Verse</h2><div class="chart short" id="trait-verse"></div></section>
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>First person</h2><div class="chart short" id="trait-first_person"></div></section>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
